    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**, 56 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, including the new `Cp45Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the salutation feature following the existing derived-field conventions in this Spring Boot / OpenAPI-generated PetClinic app.\n\n**What the change does:** the create endpoint accepts an optional `title` (e.g. MR/MRS/MS/DR), stores it, and the owner read model exposes a derived `salutation` = `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given.\n\n**Files changed:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `title` string to the `OwnerFields` schema (request/stored field) and a read-only derived `salutation` to the `Owner` schema. The `*Dto` classes are generated from this spec at build time.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persisted `title` field (`@Column(name = \"title\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"salutation\", ...)` and a `salutation(Owner)` method that composes `title + \" \" + lastName`, falling back to `lastName` when the title is null/blank. MapStruct maps the incoming `title` onto the entity automatically (same field name).\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,postgres,mysql}/schema.sql`) \u2014 added a `title` column to the `owners` table so the value persists across create \u2192 get. Tests run on the `hsqldb` profile; I updated all four for consistency.\n\nI made `title` a plain string (with the allowed values documented) rather than a strict enum, so the title is echoed back verbatim into the salutation exactly as the spec describes (\"title + ' ' + lastName\").",
